    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1096">

                <pb facs="1173" n="1077" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg1077"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Loomis to Mr.
                            Sherman.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-03-15"><hi rendition="#italic">March 15,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 99.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In reference to the disaster to the United
                    States ship of war <hi rendition="#italic">Maine</hi>, I have the honor to
                    report that all of the foreign ministers have taken occasion to express their
                    sense of regret and sorrow to me <pb facs="1174" n="1078" xml:id="pg1078"/> in a
                    very earnest, sincere, and satisfactory way, save the ministers of Italy and
                    Spain, who have said nothing.</p>
                <p>The English and German ministers called personally at the legation within two or
                    three hours after the news of the loss of the <hi rendition="#italic">Maine</hi>
                    was confirmed.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis B. Loomis.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
